client specs	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:36:27.1351609Z Note: a multi-user installation is possible. See https://nix.dev/manual/nix/stable/installation/installing-binary.html#multi-user-installation
client specs	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:36:27.1362100Z ^[[1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer^[[0m
client specs	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:36:27.1466019Z ^[[32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
client specs	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:36:27.1475767Z ^[[0m
client specs	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:36:27.1476446Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
client specs	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:36:27.1477266Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
client specs	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:36:27.1477648Z 
client specs	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:36:27.1478003Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
client specs	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:36:27.1479747Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
client specs	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:36:27.1480262Z 
client specs	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:36:27.1480600Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
client specs	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:36:27.1481298Z    if you are ready to continue.
client specs	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:36:27.1481632Z 
client specs	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:36:27.1482221Z 3. Create the system users ^[[34m(uids [30001..30008])^[[0m and groups ^[[34m(gid 30000)^[[0m
client specs	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:36:27.1483007Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
client specs	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:36:27.1483818Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
client specs	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:36:27.1484243Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
client specs	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:36:27.1484435Z 
client specs	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:36:27.1484713Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
client specs	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:36:27.1485049Z 
client specs	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:36:27.1485308Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
client specs	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:36:27.1485773Z    can use Nix.
client specs	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:36:27.1485956Z 
client specs	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:36:27.1486084Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
client specs	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:36:27.1486279Z 
client specs	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:36:27.1486616Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
client specs	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:36:27.1487161Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
client specs	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:36:27.1488061Z 
client specs	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:36:27.1488271Z I will:
client specs	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:36:27.1488679Z 
client specs	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:36:27.1489584Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
client specs	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:36:27.1490442Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
client specs	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:36:27.1491466Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
client specs	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:36:27.1492270Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
client specs	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:36:27.1492803Z  - install Nix in /nix
client specs	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:36:27.1493553Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
client specs	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:36:27.1494296Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
client specs	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:36:27.1495001Z    /root
client specs	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:36:27.1503866Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
client specs	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:36:27.1504693Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
client specs	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:36:27.1516241Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
client specs	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:36:27.1517032Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
client specs	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:36:27.1517545Z 
client specs	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:36:27.1518384Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mReady to continue?
client specs	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:36:27.1519074Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
client specs	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:36:27.1537342Z 
client specs	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:36:27.1538071Z ^[[34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
client specs	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:36:27.1548490Z ^[[0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
client specs	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:36:27.1549588Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
client specs	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:36:27.1550380Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
client specs	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:36:27.1550808Z 
client specs	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:36:27.1551149Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
client specs	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:36:27.1551630Z 
client specs	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:36:27.1551991Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
client specs	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:36:27.1552971Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
client specs	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:36:27.1553566Z 
client specs	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:36:27.1553799Z If you would like to
client specs	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:36:27.1554105Z see the output, try like this:
client specs	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:36:27.1554297Z 
client specs	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:36:27.1554534Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
client specs	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:36:27.1554951Z   $ sh ./install-nix
client specs	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:36:27.1555122Z 
client specs	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:36:27.1555155Z 
